{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01RRYQ6LVoUCBwHW2rMb1kje","input":{"command":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" && gh pr edit 2 --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdds `src/adapters/opencode.ts`, wired into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the public library surface.\n\n## Why it looks different from the other two\n\nopencode is the first source with no append-only transcript file — sessions live in a mutable SQLite DB at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Rather than read that DB, capture shells out to `opencode export --pure <id>`:\n\n- cledger has zero runtime deps and supports Node >= 20; `node:sqlite` would force both to change.\n- The schema is visibly mid-migration (an empty `session_message` table sits beside the populated `message`/`part` tables it evidently replaces).\n- That same DB holds `credential.value` and `account.access_token`. Reading conversations shouldn't mean opening the file that stores API tokens.\n\n`--sanitize` is deliberately not passed — cledger does its own redaction, and letting opencode rewrite content would make event ids depend on opencode's version.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**One event per part, not per message.** The store is mutable and a message accumulates parts over time. A part is the finest unit that stops changing, so a message that gains parts after an early `session.idle` appends rather than re-emitting changed content under a new id. Unsettled (`running`) tool calls are skipped *and* hold the cursor back, so they're captured once they finish rather than skipped forever.\n\n**Reasoning is visible, not opaque.** opencode stores reasoning as plain text, unlike Codex's provider-encrypted `encrypted_content`. So it becomes an ordinary `thinking` block in a `conversation_turn` — no opacity marker, nothing withheld.\n\n**Model recorded on user messages too.** opencode states the model on user messages; claude-code doesn't, and there none is invented. Here the source states it, so it's recorded.\n\n**Conservative type classification.** Only `text`/`reasoning`/`tool` are claimed convertible and only `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` deliberately skipped. The `file`, `agent`, `snapshot` and `todo` types opencode's binary references are left unclassified on purpose — they route through the drift path (preserved raw-only, warned about, upgradeable by `cledger renormalize`) instead of being discarded on a guess.\n\n**Subagent sessions skipped**, matching claude-code's sidechain handling. Doing it properly is a cross-adapter schema question, now on the roadmap.\n\n## Upstream bug worked around\n\n`opencode export` exits without draining a piped stdout, silently truncating at ~64KB — and the truncated JSON can still parse, so this would have quietly captured partial conversations. The child now writes to a temp file. Verified: 65516 bytes over a pipe vs 446703 to a file descriptor.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Automated:** 170 tests pass (169 + 1 pre-existing skip: `gitleaks oracle`, which needs gitleaks installed). 5 new adapter tests cover conversion, drift preservation, `occurred_at` fallbacks, idempotent re-capture, unsettled-tool cursor hold, subagent skip, and tool errors.\n\n**Live in the opencode TUI**, two-turn session against a real model:\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| human turns | `actor.type=human`, `actor.id` = git email |\n| assistant turns | `actor.id` = model |\n| plaintext reasoning | `thinking` blocks, not opaque `reasoning` events |\n| tool call | `tool_use` + `tool_result` in one event |\n| provenance | `model`/`provider`/`source_version` on every event, user turns included |\n| skipped bookkeeping | seq gaps at 1,4,5,8,10 = `step-start`/`step-finish` |\n| drift | zero `unrecognized` events |\n\nRe-capturing the same session into a different repo after deleting the original working directory produced byte-identical events with identical seqs — confirming ids are content-derived and repo-independent.\n\nA probe plugin captured a live `session.idle`, which states the session id at `properties.sessionID`. The plugin is now pinned to that field and the three speculative fallback keys are gone.\n\n## Known gaps (on the roadmap)\n\n- `conversation.seq` is positional over a mutable store, so a `session revert` can shift positions and duplicate the parts after the deletion. Per-part capture keeps the blast radius small. Untested against an actual revert.\n- The hook's most-recently-updated-session fallback (for a future opencode that renames `sessionID`) has never run in anger and deserves a test plus a warning when it triggers.\n- Attachments (`file` parts) are untested — no sample available; they'd surface as a drift warning rather than being dropped.\n- Unrelated, found while testing and recorded in the roadmap for a separate PR: `printJsonl` has no stdout `error` handler, so `cledger export | head` throws an unhandled `EPIPE` on any ledger above the 64KB pipe buffer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YZSeAzTwQ9ikr7D6aiZ8vq\nEOF\n)\" && gh pr view 2 --json isDraft,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,commits -q '\"draft=\\(.isDraft) mergeable=\\(.mergeable) state=\\(.mergeStateStatus) commits=\\(.commits|length)\"'","description":"Update PR body and confirm state"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"fae79dee09836037794eb7b34122fc5014cfaee0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":666},"id":"ev1-633294a17c19bfb30af43c82d7ac199279dd24e6223963f7e2a9ecae729bf918","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-03T03:50:13.055Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-a